---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { company, analyticsEnabled, GA_MEASUREMENT_ID, cloudflareAnalyticsEnabled, anyAnalyticsEnabled } from '../../config';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="Information on the processing of personal data on the website of ELCON LED GmbH pursuant to Art. 13 GDPR."
>
  <p class="legal-missing">
    This page is an English courtesy translation of the German privacy policy. In
    the event of any discrepancy, the
    <a href="/datenschutz/" hreflang="de" lang="de">German version</a> prevails.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    The controller for data processing on this website within the meaning of the General Data
    Protection Regulation (GDPR) is:
  </p>
  <p>
    {company.name}<br />
    {company.street}<br />
    {company.zip} {company.city}<br />
    Germany<br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${company.phoneHref}`}>{company.phone}</a><br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    No data protection officer has been appointed, as the statutory requirements for this do not
    apply. For data protection matters, please contact us at the address given above.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA,
    using the “Cloudflare Pages” service. When the website is accessed, Cloudflare processes
    technical connection data in order to deliver the page and to secure its operation. The legal
    basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest lies in the secure and efficient operation of
    the website. A data processing agreement pursuant to Art. 28 GDPR is in place with Cloudflare.
    Any transfer to the USA is based on the EU standard contractual clauses and on the provider’s
    certification under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Server log files</h2>
  <p>
    When the website is accessed, information transmitted by your browser is recorded automatically.
    This is in particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the page or file requested</li>
    <li>the date and time of the request</li>
    <li>the volume of data transferred and notification of successful retrieval</li>
    <li>browser type and version, and the operating system used</li>
    <li>the IP address of the requesting device</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This data is not merged with other data sources and serves solely for technical delivery and for
    defending against attacks. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Getting in touch</h2>
  <p>
    The enquiry form on this website does not transmit any data to our server. When you submit it,
    your local email program opens with a prepared message which you send yourself. The details you
    have entered therefore only leave your device when that email is sent, and are transmitted via
    your own email provider.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you contact us by email, telephone or fax, we process the data you provide in order to deal
    with your request. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the enquiry is aimed at concluding
    or performing a contract, and otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR on the basis of our legitimate
    interest in responding to enquiries. We delete this data once it is no longer required for the
    purpose; statutory retention periods, in particular under commercial and tax law, remain
    unaffected.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    This website uses the typefaces “Manrope” and “Inter” via the Google Fonts service provided by
    Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland. When a page is accessed,
    your browser establishes a connection to Google servers, in the course of which your IP address
    is transmitted to Google. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest lies in
    a consistent presentation of the website. Further information can be found in Google’s privacy
    policy at
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/privacy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Cookies and audience measurement</h2>
  {analyticsEnabled ? (
    <>
      <p>
        With your consent, we use Google Analytics 4 provided by Google Ireland Limited, Gordon
        House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, for audience measurement (property ID
        <code>{GA_MEASUREMENT_ID}</code>). The service uses cookies and comparable technologies that
        allow your use of the website to be analysed. The IP address is processed in truncated form
        (IP anonymisation).
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis for storing and reading information on your device is section 25(1) TDDDG,
        and for the subsequent processing Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. Consent is given via the notice shown on
        your first visit to the site and can be withdrawn at any time with effect for the future —
        using the “Cookie settings” link in the footer. We store your decision locally in your
        browser (<code>localStorage</code>) so that the notice does not reappear on every visit.
      </p>
      <p>Once consent has been given, the following is recorded in particular:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the areas of the website visited, including movement between the areas</li>
        <li>
          the source of the visit, that is the website visited beforehand and, where applicable,
          campaign parameters contained in the address
        </li>
        <li>filters used in the project overview and reference letters opened</li>
        <li>the use of buttons and of telephone, email and WhatsApp links</li>
        <li>submission of the enquiry form, including the service area selected</li>
        <li>scroll depth reached, in quarters of the page length</li>
        <li>
          technical details such as approximate location (based on the truncated IP address), device
          type, browser and screen resolution
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The content you enter into the enquiry form is not transmitted — only the fact that an
        enquiry was started, and for which service area, is recorded.
      </p>
    </>
  ) : null}

  {cloudflareAnalyticsEnabled && (
    <>
      <p>
        For audience measurement we use “Cloudflare Web Analytics” provided by Cloudflare, Inc.,
        101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. The service collects aggregated metrics on
        which pages are visited and which source visitors come from.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cloudflare Web Analytics works <strong>without cookies</strong>: no information is stored on
        or read from your device, no identifier is assigned, and there is no recognition across
        devices or websites. No usage profiles are created. For this reason, consent under section
        25(1) TDDDG is not required, and no cookie notice appears on this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        What is recorded is the address accessed, the website visited beforehand (referrer), the
        approximate region of origin at country level, and technical details about the browser,
        operating system and device type. The IP address is used for processing but is not stored.
        The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; our legitimate interest lies in designing our offering
        to meet demand and in evaluating it statistically. A data processing agreement pursuant to
        Art. 28 GDPR is in place with Cloudflare; the transfer to the USA is based on the EU standard
        contractual clauses and on the provider’s certification under the EU-US Data Privacy
        Framework.
      </p>
    </>
  )}

  {!anyAnalyticsEnabled && (
    <p>
      This website does not use any cookies for analysis, advertising or tracking purposes. No
      audience measurement takes place, no usage profiles are created and no web analytics services
      are integrated. Consent under section 25(1) TDDDG is therefore not required; for this reason,
      no cookie notice appears on this website either.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>7. Your rights as a data subject</h2>
  <p>You have the following rights in relation to your personal data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>right of access (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li>right to rectification (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li>right to erasure (Art. 17 GDPR)</li>
    <li>right to restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li>right to data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li>right to object to processing (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    <li>right to withdraw consent with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    An informal message to the contact details given under section 1 is sufficient to exercise these
    rights.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority</h2>
  <p>
    Without prejudice to any other remedies, you have the right under Art. 77 GDPR to lodge a
    complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, in particular in the Member State of
    your residence, place of work or the place of the alleged infringement. The authority
    responsible for our company is the State Commissioner for Data Protection of Lower Saxony,
    Prinzenstraße 5, 30159 Hannover, Germany.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Data security</h2>
  <p>
    This website is delivered exclusively over an encrypted connection (TLS). You can recognise this
    by the address bar of your browser, which begins with <code>https://</code>, and by the padlock
    symbol. The data transmitted between your device and our server is thus protected from access by
    third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes to this privacy policy</h2>
  <p>
    We update this privacy policy whenever changes to the procedures we use or to the legal position
    make this necessary. The version then current applies to each new visit.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
